                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "234684277",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198097473222",
                            "num_reviews": 243,
                            "playtime_forever": 86,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 86,
                            "last_played": 1788289396
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The idea is straightforward: you do not control the ball directly. Instead, you rotate and tilt the environment and politely ask physics to cooperate.\r\n\r\nSometimes it does.\r\n\r\nSometimes Orb decides gravity is merely a suggestion.\r\n\r\nThe puzzles are easy to understand, the game is simple to pick up, and while the mouse controls can be a little awkward and overly sensitive, I never found them bad enough to completely ruin the experience.\r\n\r\nThe biggest downside is that the game is very short. There are 40 levels, but you can get through them pretty quickly. Just when you start getting comfortable, the game is basically already waving goodbye.\r\n\r\nIt is also very basic visually, but it does the job. You have a ball, some platforms, some hazards, and a growing suspicion that the ball is personally trying to sabotage you.\r\n\r\nStill, for a cheap little puzzle game, I think it is perfectly fine. It is simple, occasionally frustrating, but generally enjoyable while it lasts.\r\n\r\nGameplay:\r\n\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ve3fCYZ243M",
